# Nuclei Strategy (comprehensive corpus)

**Skill:** `.cursor/skills/nuclei/SKILL.md`  
**Plan:** `.docs/docs-for-cli-tools/examination_plans/nuclei_formal_examination_plan.md`

## Principle

Do **not** pin individual templates for corpus evidence. Run the **entire template tree** (minus module exclusions) against each target and learn semantics from **which templates fire**.

## Targets

| Class | URL | Scan modes |
|-------|-----|------------|
| Permissive | `http://scanme.nmap.org` | All templates + critical/high |
| Corporate CDN | `https://www.bbc.co.uk` | All templates + critical/high |
| Corporate AU | `https://www.sbs.com.au` | Critical/high |
| Security vendor | `https://praetorian.com` | Critical/high |
| CDN edge | `https://www.cloudflare.com` | Critical/high |

## Module-equivalent flags

```
-silent -jsonl -omit-raw -omit-template
-t .tools/nuclei-templates
-no-interactsh -etags dos,fuzz,misc -duc
-retries 1 -c 25 -timeout 10
-jle <export.jsonl>
```

Add `-severity critical,high` for focused sweeps.

## Workflow

1. **Explore** — `run_nuclei_exploration.bat` (hours per target; sequential).
2. **Analyze** — `python .seed/scripts/cli_corpus/analyze_nuclei_jsonl.py <export> -o <summary.json>`
3. **Examine** — `harvest.py --tool nuclei` (7 scenarios, JSON bundles).

## Runtime expectations

- Template engine cold start ~3 min; full-tree scans **hours** per URL on ~13k templates.
- Use `-jle` file export (not stdout) for large result sets.
- Harvest timeout: 14400s (all-templates), 7200s (critical/high).

## Deferred

- Per-template examination rows (replaced by comprehensive exports)
- `cli_tool_to_graph.nuclei_to_graph` until operator approves bundles
